@startuml
title Record Study Session

actor User
boundary "StudySessionController" as Controller
control "LearningApplicationService" as App
entity "LearningGoalRepository" as GoalRepo
entity "StudySession" as Session
entity "StudySessionRepository" as SessionRepo

User -> Controller : POST /study-sessions
Controller -> App : recordStudySession(command)
App -> GoalRepo : findById(learningGoalId)
GoalRepo --> App : LearningGoal
App -> App : verify goal can accept study session
App -> Session : create(learningGoalId, studyDate, duration, content)
Session --> App : StudySession
App -> SessionRepo : save(session)
SessionRepo --> App : saved StudySession
App --> Controller : result
Controller --> User : 201 Created

note right of App
Type:
Application Service

Responsibility:
Coordinate the use case and transaction.

Business Rules:
Loads LearningGoal to avoid recording study against an invalid goal.
Delegates StudySession invariants to the domain model.

Dependencies:
Depends on domain repositories.
end note

note right of Session
Type:
Aggregate Root

Responsibility:
Validate and hold one study record.

Invariants:
Duration is positive and content is not blank.

Persistence:
Saved independently from LearningGoal.
end note

@enduml

